  "verbalization": "Palmarumycin CP18 appears to interact with 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets NCI-H2228 through multiple pathways. The drug's interaction with Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5, TE-11, and GCIY suggests a broader role in modulating the expression of downstream targets. These targets are all involved in metabolic and signaling pathways that influence cellular processes, potentially affecting the growth and survival of NCI-H2228 cells. The consistent presence of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid as a common mediator across different targets implies a central role in the drug's mechanism of action. The evidence supports a hypothesis that palmarumycin CP18 exerts its effects through a network of targets that ultimately influence NCI-H2228, highlighting a complex, multi-target interaction that may be critical for its biological activity.",
